{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789245494,"nonce":"kDwQ+uBp7yEVFK7ktiGH8vYK7wA=","title":"Folding a constant CondBranch left the dead edge's phi incomings behind","message":"`const_fold::fold_terminators` turned `brcond true, A, B` into `br A` but\nleft B's phis with their incoming from the folding block and B's\npredecessor list unchanged. `cfg_simplify` then merged the header into\nits body and rewired the body's edge to B onto the header, so B's phi\nheld two values from one block and the backend took the first, the\nvalue from before the loop.\n\nReproducer: `x = 0; while True: x = 1; break; print(x)` printed 0.\n\nFix: drop the dead target's incoming from this block and this block\nfrom its predecessors when the branch folds.","files":null}]}